+# OMB receipt leads for DOT’s FY 2006 accountability report
+
+Public derivative of the November 9, 2026 Eastern source review · B129 / PD03–PD05. The prior study recovered the public DOT report and its component PDFs. This review traces a different copy, the report and transmittal records that the 2006 OMB instructions directed to the Office of Federal Financial Management (**OFFM**) and appropriate Resource Management Office (**RMO**). Five OFFM catalog descriptions span 2006 and supply transfer numbers. The series specifically titled for accountability reports ends in 2004 and describes a different subject scope. The actual November 2006 report submission and receipt remain unacquired. [Public report recovery](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/a411674551abcca8df26584f0f1776892ed8e5cb/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-par2006-sender-package-and-omb-routing-2026-11-09/README.md)
+
+## OFFM series and limits
+
+The July 2006 circular identifies separate OFFM and RMO draft and final routes. OMB’s contemporaneous organization page describes the RMOs as program and agency-facing offices and OFFM as a financial-management policy office. Use the creator field, series scope and transfer identifiers together. A date span indicates possible coverage. The catalog leaves actual custody of the specific report open. [Circular A-136, physical pp. 9–10](https://obamawhitehouse.archives.gov/sites/default/files/omb/assets/omb/circulars/a136/a136_revised_2006.pdf#page=9) · [OMB structure, raw HTML lines 109–117 and 138–141](https://georgewbush-whitehouse.archives.gov/omb/organization/mission.html)
+
+| Series and original catalog line | Inclusive dates, transfer and access field | Why it matters |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| **Financial Management Subject Files**, `rg_51-222.jsonl` line 8 | `2001-01-01`–`2008-12-31`; `UD-18W 61`, `PT-051-2011-0013`; two cartons; `Unrestricted` | OFFM correspondence and related files in the report period. [NAID 246939526](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/246939526) |
+| **Subject Files**, `rg_51-169.jsonl` line 11 | `2001-01-01`–`2007-12-31`; `UD-18W 26`, `W051-08-0011`; five cartons; `Restricted - Possibly` | Description includes agency financial reviews, correspondence, reports and statements. [NAID 239086672](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/239086672) |
+| **Subject Files**, `rg_51-180.jsonl` line 6 | `1990-11-15`–`2006-12-31`; `UD-18W 6`, `W051-08-0013`; three cartons; `Restricted - Possibly` | Same broad scope description, different coverage and transfer. [NAID 239076104](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/239076104) |
+| **Subject Files**, `rg_51-320.jsonl` line 12 | `2001-01-01`–`2008-12-31`; `UD-18W 60`, `PT-051-2010-0024`; four cartons; `Restricted - Possibly` | The catalog adds agency disposition number `DAL-0051-2011-0021-0001`. [NAID 239232997](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/239232997) |
+| **Subject Files**, `rg_51-384.jsonl` line 7 | `1999-11-01`–`2009-01-19`; `UD-18W 53`, `PT-051-2011-0053`; four cartons; `Restricted - Possibly` | The same agency disposition field appears beside a distinct transfer and date range. [NAID 239092909](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/239092909) |
+| **Subject Files Relating to Performance and Accountability Reports**, `rg_51-361.jsonl` line 4 | `2001-01-01`–`2004-12-31`; `UD-17W 73`, `W051-05-0010`; one carton; `Restricted - Possibly` | The title looks close. The record’s own scope says `National Credit Administration and government corporations`. Preserve that wording and the 2004 endpoint. [NAID 74616330](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/74616330) |
+
+An earlier OFFM **Agency Chief Financial Officer Submission Files** series covers 1993–2000, a useful title lead with a different date boundary. A separate OMB **Program Records** series covers 2001–2006 and lists a container boundary from Transportation to Veterans Affairs. Its creator is the **Office of Information and Regulatory Affairs**, a different route from the OFFM/RMO instructions. The container boundary is descriptive and supplies no item-level evidence of a FY 2006 DOT PAR. Two bare `Department of Transportation` file-unit titles in the snapshot are respectively under hiring-freeze and workplace-safety records. Their parent fields illustrate why title and agency alone are insufficient. [Earlier CFO submissions](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/74616268) · [OIRA program records](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/74616323) · [Hiring-freeze folder](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/117681107) · [Workplace-safety folder](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/100360177)
+
+## RMO schedule boundary
+
+- **DAA-0051-2015-0001.** The RMO Review and Oversight item **0001** lists agency review records and cites predecessor **NC1-51-79-3, item 3**. The permanent RMO Publications item **0002** and Budget Submissions and Strategic Plan item **0005** each show `2009` as the first accumulation year and `From 2009 To 2017` as the planned initial transfer span. Those fields leave the 2006 submission outside the stated accumulation range for those two series. [Approved schedule, physical pp. 4–7](https://www.archives.gov/files/records-mgmt/rcs/schedules/executive-office-of-the-president/rg-0051/daa-0051-2015-0001_sf115.pdf#page=4)
+- **NC1-051-79-03.** The older Transportation, Commerce, and Housing Division schedule lists separate permanent Transportation Branch **Program Records**, item 11, and **Budgetary Records**, item 12. Item 11 uses a two-year cutoff and item 12 a fiscal-year cutoff. Both list EOP Depository and FRC transfer language at two years old and offer to NARS at eight years old. Keep those instructions and the distinct cutoffs as printed. The NARA notice dated August 9, 2022 lists supersessions for **items 3 and 9**. The public guide’s named Transportation Branch program holdings stop at `1969-76` in its historical entry. The legacy office lineage, applicable disposition authority and the specific 2006 transfer remain unverified. [Older schedule, physical pp. 1 and 6](https://www.archives.gov/files/records-mgmt/rcs/schedules/executive-office-of-the-president/rg-0051/nc1-051-79-03_sf115.pdf#page=6) · [Historical guide, §51.9.13](https://www.archives.gov/research/guide-fed-records/groups/051.html)
+
+## Verification and next discriminator
+
+Verified six source responses, the held A-136 hash, and the SHA-256 of all **400 objects** in the captured nontruncated RG 51 prefix, then parsed their **3,423 descriptions**. Selected eleven descriptions carry exact JSONL line numbers, byte hashes and separate dates, creators and access fields. None has a linked digital object or indexed descendant in this snapshot. The bounded search of title, scope and container-list fields produced no exact combined DOT FY 2006 PAR or investigation-key match. Series contents and separately held, restricted or undescribed material were outside that search. [Exact pins and verification](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+**TODO:** Start with the container inventories and November 2006 OFFM incoming registers for **UD-18W 61 / PT-051-2011-0013**, **UD-18W 26 / W051-08-0011** and the distinct subject transfers. Match any submission by signed cover or control number, final electronic attachment and receipt, then compare it to the recovered public report and House 10204 and Senate EC–9158 packets. Establish the 2006 transportation RMO’s actual filing route separately. The corrected FAA answer and receipt, signed administrative decision and recommendation-specific implementation and closure remain open. [House and Senate referral comparison](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/af53c3c57d15a6e76ce8beb468e9aba9ffaf3be9/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-house-10204-receiving-register-2026-11-09/README.md)
